<title>USA: USDA ATTACHE REPORT ON FRENCH RAPESEED CROP.</title>
<headline>USDA ATTACHE REPORT ON FRENCH RAPESEED CROP.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The USDA attache in Paris filed the following report, dated Aug 7, on the French rapeseed crop.</p>
<p>The area planted to rapeseed in 1997/98 has been revised from 940,000 ha in report FR9706A to 960,000 ha. According to the French Interprofessional Society for Oilseeds and Pulses (SIDO), this area is broken down into 160,000 ha of industrial rapeseed and 800,000 ha of food/feed rapeseed.</p>
<p>Although the revised area is higher, total French rapeseed production in 1997/98 is not likely to exceed 3 million MT,due to unfavorable weather conditions in 1997, including drought in April and heavy rains in June. Commodity: Oilseed, Rapeseed (2226000) (1000 HECTARES)(1000 MT)</p>
